    "title": "Woman pleads not guilty to obstruction in controversial Elyria arrest - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Owen MacMillan Bruce Bishop The Chronicle-Telegram ,\n4 hours ago ELYRIA — An Elyria woman has pleaded not guilty after being charged with interfering in an arrest of a 15-year-old girl after a Juneteenth celebration in Ely Square. Ciera Ramon, 48, of Elyria was arraigned before Elyria Municipal Judge Robert White on Wednesday and pleaded not guilty to misdemeanor charges of obstruction of justice and resisting arrest. Read full article",
